id: ops-packed-network-options
title: Keep the configured network-family timeout in packed consumer installs
description: "Round AX verified that test/continuation-selection.acceptance.ts builds a sanitized child environment without NODE_OPTIONS. With degraded network access, the initial npm consumer install exceeded its 240-second bound despite the caller exporting --network-family-autoselection-attempt-timeout=5000. Retrying the unchanged test through a temporary npm launcher that restores only that option passed both npm and native Bun consumers on identical tarball sha256 e43ad16bb909ddd15ef0def4e49f5345e803346f61dcef20809cdadca058245b. Preserve the explicit network-family timeout at the install boundary while retaining credential isolation and avoiding arbitrary preload options."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 3
tags[2]: "area:release","area:tests"
created_at: "2026-11-17T15:29:20.026Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-17T15:29:24.536Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: A regression proves the explicit network-family timeout reaches npm installs through the sanitized fixture environment; unrelated inherited variables and arbitrary preload flags remain excluded; unchanged packed npm and Bun acceptance passes.
